  "html": "<section id=\"highlights\"><div class=\"sect\"><h2>Research Highlights</h2></div><div class=\"highlights\"><article><div class=\"peregrine-figures\"><a class=\"research-figure\" href=\"assets/peregrine-overview.png\" aria-label=\"Enlarge Peregrine overview figure\"><img class=\"research-image\" src=\"assets/peregrine-overview.png\" alt=\"Peregrine computes features before downsampling, preserving information from all packets for ML-based detection\" loading=\"lazy\"></a><a class=\"research-figure\" href=\"assets/peregrine-summary-4.png\" aria-label=\"Enlarge Peregrine detection quality and throughput comparison\"><img class=\"research-image\" src=\"assets/peregrine-summary-4.png\" alt=\"Detection quality versus supported network rate for Peregrine and other detectors; click to view the full chart, including experimental conditions and backend capacity assumptions\" loading=\"lazy\"></a></div><span class=\"meta\">[Preprint 2026] Peregrine</span><h3><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2403.18788\">Where to Sample: Rethinking ML-Based Malicious Traffic Detection at Terabit Scale</a></h3><p>Computing ML features over all packets before sampling, then sending fewer feature records to software inference—preserving detection effectiveness at terabit scale.</p><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2403.18788\">Read the paper →</a></article><article><span class=\"meta\">[HotNets 2024] Internet architecture</span><h3><a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1145/3696348.3696876\">Found in Translation</a></h3><p>Exploring how translation can help the Internet evolve towards new architectures.</p><a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1145/3696348.3696876\">Read the paper →</a></article><article><a class=\"research-figure\" href=\"assets/maestro-architecture.png\" aria-label=\"Enlarge Maestro architecture figure\"><img class=\"research-image\" src=\"assets/maestro-architecture.png\" alt=\"Maestro architecture: sequential network function, symbolic execution, constraints generation, RSS configuration and parallel code generation\" loading=\"lazy\"></a><span class=\"meta\">[NSDI 2024] Maestro</span><h3><a href=\"https://maestro.inesc-id.pt/\">Automatic parallelization of network functions</a></h3><p>Turning sequential network functions into parallel implementations while preserving their semantics.</p><a href=\"https://www.usenix.org/conference/nsdi24/presentation/pereira\">Paper & presentation →</a></article></div></section>"
